<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7644" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνᾱτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτη</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unharmed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				19
			</span></i>(cj.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αοξίου κότῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1211
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακῶν ἄνατος</span>
			<i>harmed by no</i> ills, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				786
			</span></i>, where the Laur.Ms. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄναιτος.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>not harming, harmless,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				356
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				359
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				410
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>immune from punishment,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρχ. Ἐφ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1920.76
				</span></i>
			 (Crete, <span class="entity">vi/v B.C.</span>). Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				<i>with impunity,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					IG
					9(1).333
				</span></i>
			 (
				Locr.
			). (Contr. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάατος,</span>
			q.v.)</div>
